idx\": 2 }, \"79740\": { \"order_id\": 3, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Socialization agents\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A child in a rural Ghanaian community is learning traditional values and norms. Which of the following is the <b>primary</b> agent of socialization in this context?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>The family is the primary agent of socialization, especially in rural Ghanaian communities. It is the first institution where a child learns values, norms, traditions, and cultural practices. The family shapes the child's behavior, attitudes, and worldview, laying the foundation for their social development.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68165\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"The school.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24605\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"The family.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99536\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"The mass media.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58462\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"Peer groups.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 3 }, \"79741\": { \"order_id\": 4, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Leadership styles\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A leader in a Ghanaian community consistently involves community members in decision-making processes. Which leadership style is being demonstrated?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>The democratic leadership style involves the participation of group members in decision-making processes. This style encourages collaboration, shared responsibility, and mutual respect, which are essential for effective community development. It contrasts with autocratic or laissez-faire leadership styles, where decisions are either centralized or left entirely to the group.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68166\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"Autocratic leadership.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24606\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"Democratic leadership.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99537\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"Laissez-faire leadership.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58463\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"Charismatic leadership.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 4 }, \"79742\": { \"order_id\": 5, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Ghanaian values\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>During a cultural festival in Ghana, a speaker emphasizes the importance of <i>respect for elders</i>. Which of the following <b>best</b> describes this value in Ghanaian society?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>Respect for elders is a core value in Ghanaian society. It reflects the cultural emphasis on hierarchy, wisdom, and the transmission of knowledge and traditions from older generations to younger ones. This value fosters social cohesion, intergenerational harmony, and the preservation of cultural heritage.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68167\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"A modern concept introduced by Western education.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24607\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"A traditional value that promotes social cohesion and intergenerational harmony.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99538\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"A legal requirement enforced by the government.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58464\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"A value that discourages individual achievement.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 5 }, \"79743\": { \"order_id\": 6, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Change in Ghana\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A village in Ghana is transitioning from traditional farming methods to modern agricultural techniques. Which of the following is a <b>likely</b> challenge they may face during this change?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>Resistance to change is a common challenge when communities transition from traditional to modern practices. This resistance may stem from fear of the unknown, attachment to cultural practices, lack of resources, or skepticism about the benefits of modern techniques. Overcoming such resistance requires education, community engagement, and gradual implementation of new methods.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68168\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"Increased acceptance of traditional beliefs.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24608\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"Resistance from community members due to fear of the unknown.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99539\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"Immediate economic prosperity for all villagers.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58465\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"A decline in cultural festivals and celebrations.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 6 }, \"79744\": { \"order_id\": 7, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Social control types\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>In a Ghanaian community, a person who steals is publicly reprimanded and made to compensate the victim. Which type of social control is being applied?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>Informal social control refers to the mechanisms used by communities to regulate behavior without formal legal systems. Public reprimand and restitution are examples of informal social control, as they rely on community norms, values, and social pressure to enforce conformity and maintain order.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68169\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"Formal social control.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24609\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"Informal social control.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99540\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"Legal social control.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58466\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"Economic social control.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 7 }, \"79745\": { \"order_id\": 8, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Leadership and followership\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A leader in a Ghanaian organization is known for making decisions without consulting followers. How might this leadership style affect followership in the organization?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>An autocratic leadership style, where decisions are made unilaterally by the leader, often leads to reduced morale, lack of initiative, and passive followership. Followers may feel disempowered, undervalued, or demotivated, which can hinder productivity and innovation within the organization. Effective leadership requires balancing authority with inclusivity to foster active and engaged followership.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68170\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"It encourages active participation and innovation among followers.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24610\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"It may lead to reduced morale and passive followership.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99541\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"It ensures that all followers are equally rewarded.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58467\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"It eliminates the need for followership in the organization.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 8 }, \"79746\": { \"order_id\": 9, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Personal hygiene guide\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A teacher is educating students on the importance of personal hygiene. Which of the following <b>best</b> explains why personal hygiene is essential for individual and community health?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>Personal hygiene is crucial for preventing the spread of diseases, maintaining good health, and promoting overall well-being. Practices such as regular handwashing, bathing, and proper waste disposal reduce the risk of infections and contribute to a healthier community. Good hygiene habits also foster self-respect and social acceptance.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68171\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"It ensures that individuals always look attractive.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24611\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"It prevents the spread of diseases and promotes overall well-being.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99542\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"It guarantees success in academic and professional life.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58468\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"It eliminates the need for medical care.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 9 }, \"79747\": { \"order_id\": 10, \"exam_type\": \"WAEC\", \"subject\": \"Social Studies\", \"topic\": \"Social studies in development\", \"question_type\": \"Practical\", \"exam_year\": \"2004\", \"question_text\": \"<p>A development planner in Ghana is using social studies principles to design a community project. How does social studies contribute to national development?</p>\", \"question_image\": null, \"answer_image\": null, \"explanation\": \"<p>Social studies provides a multidisciplinary approach to understanding societal issues, cultural dynamics, and human behavior. It equips development planners with the knowledge and skills to design inclusive, sustainable, and culturally sensitive projects. By addressing social, economic, and political challenges, social studies fosters informed decision-making and promotes holistic national development.</p>\", \"reference_passage\": null, \"novel\": null, \"comments_count\": 0, \"options\": [ { \"option_id\": \"68172\", \"tag\": \"a\", \"text\": \"It focuses solely on economic growth without considering social factors.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"24612\", \"tag\": \"b\", \"text\": \"It provides a framework for understanding societal issues and designing inclusive development projects.\", \"is_correct\": true }, { \"option_id\": \"99543\", \"tag\": \"c\", \"text\": \"It prioritizes technological advancement over cultural preservation.\", \"is_correct\": false }, { \"option_id\": \"58469\", \"tag\": \"d\", \"text\": \"It discourages community participation in development initiatives.\", \"is_correct\": false } ], \"_page_num\": 1, \"_page_idx\": 10 } }```json```}```  (Note: The outer ```json``` and ``` markers are for display purposes only and should not be included in the actual output.)  Here is the corrected and properly formatted JSON output without any additional text or markers:  ```json  {     ": {
